## Setup

```bash
uv sync                  # install the package and the dev tools
uv run pre-commit install
```

Tell [experimaestro](https://experimaestro-python.readthedocs.io/en/latest/settings/)
where to store the outputs in `~/.config/experimaestro/settings.yaml`:

```yaml
workspaces:
  - id: {{ project_name }}
    path: ~/experiments/{{ project_name }}
    triggers:
      - "{{ project_name }}-*"
```

To run on a SLURM cluster, also add a
[`launchers.py`](https://experimaestro-python.readthedocs.io/en/latest/launchers/)
file next to it.

## Experiments

```bash
# Check the task graph without running anything
uv run experimaestro run --run-mode dry_run experiments/{{ experiment_name }}/{{ specifications[0] }}.yaml

# Run (the process schedules the jobs and waits for them)
uv run experimaestro run experiments/{{ experiment_name }}/{{ specifications[0] }}.yaml
```

See [docs/experiments.md](docs/experiments.md) for the details.

## Development

```bash
uv run pytest
```

Commit messages follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)
(`feat: …`, `fix: …`), enforced by a pre-commit hook. To avoid failed commits
when the hooks reformat files:

```bash
git add <files> && uv run pre-commit; git add -u && git commit -m "..."
```

